      "CRYSTAL: She doesn’t know the sound of her own voice, her infinite beauty. She’s half-note scattered without rhythm, no tune. Sing her sighs... Sing …\nALICE/JUANITA: And this is for colored girls who have considered suicide but moved to the ends of their own rainbows.",
      "KELLY: Hello.\nCRYSTAL: Yes.\nKELLY: Hi, I’m Kelly Watkins from Child Welfare.",
      "CRYSTAL: What can I do for you?\nKELLY: I’m looking for Crystal Wallace.\nCRYSTAL: What do you want with her?\nKELLY: I don’t have time to play these games Ms. Wallace. Open the door or I’m coming back with the police.",
