    "bookends": {
      "first": {
        "speaker": 4,
        "line": 3,
        "text": "Dark phrases of womanhood, of never having been a girl. Half-note scattered without rhythm."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 3,
        "line": 955,
        "text": "I sat up one night walking my apartment floors screaming, crying. The ghost of another woman who was missing what I was missing I wanted to jump outta my bones and be done with myself. Leave me alone and go on in the wind. It was too much."
      }
